ms on these guys  that again I don't know if they are  actually military but they're kitted out  and acting like military you know  they're all tactical and they've got  full gear and all this stuff  and while it was good  since seen don't get me wrong and the  the the fight looked good and everything  that pinged my radar right there it's  like why is he fighting soldiers and  that because I see that and I think that  that doesn't feel like Frank castle that  feels like Jason Bourne and I I don't  know if that's a good compare and I  don't mean like it's suddenly gonna be  born Chinese opera but I just mean the  guy who was betrayed by the government  taking on that government like that's  that's not Frank's story and I do  understand he's dealt with military  people he's taken on you know dictators  in foreign countries and this and that  and he's dealt with crooked military I  understand that's been there but what is  the fundamental root of what the  punishments the Punishers and war on  crime so the first season of his own  show should be his war on crime you  could do a him dealing with you know a  corrupt military organization or a  private military contractor or you know  corrupt individuals in homeland secure  or whatever like in a second season the  first season do do the fundamentals of  the character and the fundamentals of  the Punisher is man makes war against  crime street-level crime gritty crime  the kind of crime that just you was  investing New York in the 70s and 80s  when the character was first introduced  there was really only one moment in this  whole trailer that felt like a true  Punisher moment to me he's pointing the  gun at this guy on the ground who's  obviously unarmed and no longer a threat  he says what do you know about my family  the guy says I don't know anything  he says fair enough and shoots him  anyway that is the Punisher that's Frank  Castle and that's the only moment where  I really felt like that was him because  again jus